===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*krewh₂-}}
Existing in English since the sixteenth century: from {{der|en|la|pancreas}}, from {{der|en|grc|πάγκρεας}}, from {{m|grc|πᾶν|t=all}} (equivalent to English {{m|en|pan-}}) + {{m|grc|κρέας|t=flesh}}.<ref name="COED-etym">The '''Concise Oxford English Dictionary''', 11<sup>th</sup> ed.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpæŋkɹɪəs/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-pancreas.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpæŋ.kɹi.əs/|/ˈpeɪŋ-/|/ˈpæn-/|/ˈpeɪn-/|a=US}}

===Noun===
[[File:Deutsche Welle - Explaining The Human Body (English) - The Pancreas Keeping Our Blood Sugar Level in Check.webm|thumb|upright|explainer video about the human pancreas]]
{{en-noun|+|pancreata}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A [[gland]] near the [[stomach]] which [[secrete]]s a [[fluid]] into the [[duodenum]] to [[assist]] with [[food]] [[digestion]].
#: {{syn|en|gutbread|stomach sweetbread|belly sweetbread}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Maxine Lipner|title=What Does It Mean When Your Poop Floats?|magazine={{w|Health (magazine)|Health}}|url=https://www.health.com/condition/digestive-health/what-does-it-mean-when-your-poop-floats|date=2024-10-09|passage=Chronic pancreatitis is a condition in which the '''pancreas''' is inflamed or swells for an extended period.}}

